Peer testimonials and user reviews shape purchasing decisions and build confidence in product quality and brand reliability, especially for reused or alternative consumption models. Social proof from users communicating real experiences with durability, repairability, and satisfaction proves more persuasive than corporate claims. Peer testimonials provide authentic evidence about product longevity, facilitating consumer preference for designed-to-last products. From a circular perspective, positive peer testimonials about used product quality directly enable reuse markets to grow by reducing transaction risk and information asymmetry.